Subject: [M149] media: Invalidate dependent PPS when SPS is overwritten

Original change's description:
> media: Invalidate dependent PPS when SPS is overwritten
>
> In the H.264 and H.265 parsers, overwriting an existing SPS left
> dependent PPS active. This could lead to an inconsistent state where
> a PPS bypasses validation checks against the new SPS geometry,
> potentially causing out-of-bounds math in downstream hardware delegates.
>
> This change fixes the issue by erasing dependent PPSes when their parent
> SPS is overwritten, safely failing the decoder on subsequent slices
> until a new, valid PPS is provided.
>
